From 1d4570b1f1d8de604a567bed08fb755060a1fdb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick <nick@rudrabiz.dev>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:58:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve merge conflicts; make received-cheques filter strip a
 single compact line

- public/index.html, style.css, public/js/received.js, routes/cheques.js had
  unresolved <<<<<<< ours/======/>>>>>>> theirs markers checked into HEAD.
  Resolved in favor of the 'theirs' side throughout (sortable columns,
  date-range filter, compact filter-strip layout) - it was the more complete
  and mutually consistent branch across all four files.
- Flattened the received-cheques filter bar from a two-row layout into one
  flat line, smaller type/padding, so it reads as a hairline of chrome and
  the table gets essentially all of the panel's height.
- Added a sticky table header for the received-cheques ledger while scrolling.
- No changes to table columns, row markup, cell content, or JS logic beyond
  the conflict resolution itself.
